Input: {"question": "Which person or organization did Dawn Lonsinger work for?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 181, "text": "As Dawn Lonsinger sipped her mint tea on the sun-drenched balcony of her Tunisian apartment, she gazed out at the sprawling campus of the Institute of Press and Information Science."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 182, "end": 342, "text": "The morning light cast a warm glow on the modern architecture, and the sound of chirping birds mingled with the distant hum of students hurrying to their 8 a.m."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 343, "end": 352, "text": "lectures."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 353, "end": 479, "text": "It was a familiar scene, one she'd grown to love during her three years as an Assistant Professor of English at the institute."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 480, "end": 616, "text": "Dawn's thoughts drifted back to the previous evening's faculty gathering, where she'd engaged in a lively debate with her colleague, Dr."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 617, "end": 683, "text": "Amir, about the role of social media in shaping modern journalism."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 684, "end": 891, "text": "Their discussion had spilled over into the courtyard, where the scent of jasmine and orange blossoms filled the air, and the stars twinkling above seemed to underscore the significance of their conversation."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 892, "end": 926, "text": "As she prepared for her own 9 a.m."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 927, "end": 1042, "text": "lecture on Postcolonial Literature, Dawn's mind wandered to the stack of papers on her desk, awaiting her feedback."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1043, "end": 1171, "text": "She was